83c4465eedd95d14d9fdab9cec0b148837eb8187a03c76bd41d","event_uuid":"c7d4c738-7dea-461c-a3fb-cdef8db567ed","position":{"commit_sha":"cd6695772f5ebaf20e4cefb15d694f959c29e327","position":"1787303417448327001-c7d4c738-7dea-461c-a3fb-cdef8db567ed"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"5e3fff357a87c32a26ca507bec20f1e1e1371f5305b59d0fb1476fda7cf30ca5","event_uuid":"c59478c4-0874-4422-b3a9-ebc602d20ad3","position":{"commit_sha":"f93c87e2aba3f3e02f8ead2ac3b238093e63b8c7","position":"1787303461916732001-c59478c4-0874-4422-b3a9-ebc602d20ad3"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"7d134ac1ed4d8ea04e4efc8436818d3436295f8118f89a1bc63fef2788988bac","event_uuid":"2c9048b4-35b4-4222-a6a6-71609f1ae6ae","position":{"commit_sha":"ce323401d374e99358401f0c365b31d84e0223f0","position":"1787303463845987001-2c9048b4-35b4-4222-a6a6-71609f1ae6ae"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"S3 complete — merged as Gerrit change 1988 (LLM-Review+1 & Verified+1), merged SHA be8a60ba11. AC evidence (codebase-verified):\n\nAC1 (one lazy handler per command via a closed adapter kind; only selected modules imported): every core/bridge route in _registry.ROUTES now carries handler+adapter+init (audit/config/reconcile/etc. keep handler=None — intercept ladder untouched); ADAPTER_KINDS is the closed set {dispatcher,argv,argv_tracker,argv_tracker_root}. Proven by test_cli_registry_dispatch: dispatch_routes_carry_a_closed_adapter_and_init_policy, every_adapter_kind_has_at_least_one_route, the per-adapter typed-fake tests, and dispatching_a_read_imports_no_unrelated_handler_or_optional_stack (subprocess: CLEAN — no bridge/transition/reconciler/pydantic_ai leak).\n\nAC2 (remainder argv preserved; selected S2 factory parses exactly once; no route-level grammar): _execute._invoke passes the remainder unchanged and never parses; test_selected_factory_parses_exactly_once_and_unrelated_stay_unimported (build_show called 1x, build_list never imported) and test_router_delegates_core_dispatch_to_the_executor.\n\nAC3 (registry-derived mount/init matches the pre-cutover census incl. no-auto-mount + conditional): init policy per route pinned by test_route_init_policy_matches_pre_cutover_census (27 routes) + the none/init_only/full spies + the doctor and fsck_recover conditional selectors + the export/import split; _store_mount_eligible + _NO_AUTO_MOUNT unchanged; test_central_mount_gate_ad9f green (incl. no_store_command_is_not_force_mounted, help/unknown do not mount).\n\nAC4 (confirmation, global output extraction, legacy JSON, --, streams, exit codes, exceptions): the _dispatch_confirmable overlay (global --output/--quiet extraction, legacy --output re-injection, confirmation_context) is retained verbatim; test_confirmable_verb_preserves_tokens_after_double_dash, test_malformed_global_output_flag_on_confirmable_verb_exits_two, test_legacy_output_verbs_reinject_the_extracted_format, test_handler_exception_propagates_out_of_execute; test_cli_argparse / test_cli_space_form_options / test_leaf_writes_parity green.\n\nAC5 (bridge compat + hidden bridge-status via approved adapters; purge-bridge unknown): bridge-status routes via the argv adapter with argv_prefix=(\"status\",); test_bridge_status_prefixes_status_through_the_bridge_adapter, test_bridge_canonical_passes_the_remainder_verbatim, test_purge_bridge_remains_unknown; test_bridge_vocabulary_heldout + test_bridge_status_heldout green.\n\nAC6 (switch back to derived compatibility exports without handler/help/data changes): the literal policy frozensets and _DERIVED_POLICY_SETS remain the compatibility exports; derive_policy_sets() reproduces the live router with zero delta (test_cli_registry) and test_derived_policy_sets_still_reproduce_the_live_frozensets. No event/ticket/bridge/help/persisted-data change.\n\nRegistry validate() gained execution-metadata checks (unknown_adapter/unknown_init/handler_without_adapter/prefix_without_argv), each with an adversarial detection-path test (teeth verified). Full held-out oracle 60/60 green; mutation of the dispatcher name-prefix and the doctor selector both went RED. make lint/typecheck/complexity-baseline clean; module sizes __init__=535, _registry=707, _execute=82 (<800 cap).","timestamp":1787303402361279001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"FORCE_CLOSE: close gate(s) bypassed by user approval — no completion/signature attestation was signed. Reason: \"Plan-review staleness triggered only by a mechanical file_impact append (declaring the new executor src/rebar/_cli/_execute.py and the compatibility-allowlist test file I touched), not a material re-plan. The re-review BLOCK (G1G2) faults the plan for not enumerating Route.handler population, but it materializes the pre-implementation base SHA 9b1d2e6808 where all handlers are None; the landed change (Gerrit 1988, merged be8a60ba11, LLM-Review+1 and Verified+1) populates every core/bridge handler and passes the full held-out oracle — a provable stale-premise artifact of reviewing already-implemented code.\". Session: be8a60ba11.","timestamp":1787303463845987001}],"created_at":1787069577075394001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"bd9ec12b-f5b9-4f1c-b6c5-78caed545cc2","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"2635-4aa3-5c14-4b12"},{"link_uuid":"65f0316b-c8a7-4e10-a0ce-f61a68d8bd36","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"b06c-04a9-52b2-42fe"},{"link_uuid":"a43848aa-67b3-4774-94a1-6325ecb54f47","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"90ce-d36c-2c79-4048"},{"link_uuid":"53d58059-c1c1-4893-966e-bc3b47419ca0","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"2784-f69a-87db-4fb3"},{"link_uuid":"55efb4fd-7985-40fc-88b8-e9cc3cf44fea","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"1806-786a-1efc-484d"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nAfter S2, command identity/help and every handler grammar come from the registry/parser system, but real execution still traverses explicit intercept/dispatch ladders and policy frozensets. Leaving those selection authorities in parallel preserves the coordination defect RP-05 is intended to remove.\n\n## Approach\nMove core top-level execution to the selected registry route after the pre-operation help boundary. Resolve only the selected lazy handler reference and invoke it through a closed typed adapter-kind set matching existing call shapes. The router passes the original command remainder unchanged; the selected handler uses S2's shared argparse factory. The router must not parse command/nested options a second time.\n\nConsume route metadata for:\n\n- central best-effort mount eligibility;\n- strict initialization `none`, `init_only`, or `full`, plus narrow pure selectors for genuinely conditional cases;\n- position-independent confirmation/output extraction while preserving tokens after `--`;\n- legacy output passthrough for `create`, `idea`, `transition`, `claim`, and `reopen`;\n- exact handler adapter, argv, stdout/stderr, exit-code, and exception contracts.\n\nBefore cutover, compare registry-derived policies and selected handler/parser pairs to every existing set and arm. Any non-allowlisted delta fails shadow parity. Cut over one selection authority only after parity is exact; keep derived compatibility exports for S6 rollback.\n\nThis story covers core and bridge execution that does not change optional-capability posture. S4 owns selected optional mode/backend checks and may proceed from the same S2 contract without editing dispatch.\n\n## Compatibility and Rollback\nThe positive rationale is a single validated selection/dispatch authority while preserving specialized parser-backed handlers. No signature introspection, middleware pipeline, eager parser-tree construction, or second parse is added. Rollback selects the derived compatibility exports; no event, ticket, bridge, or binding data changes.\n\n## Testing\nUse real CLI subprocess contracts rather than source greps. Extend mount/init, mutation confirmation, global output, bridge vocabulary, hidden alias, unknown, and exit-code suites. Add typed fake handlers for every adapter kind/selector. Include negative controls for tokens after `--`, malformed global flags, no-auto-mount commands, store-touching intercepts, handler exceptions, and a parser spy proving the selected handler parses exactly once while unrelated factories/handlers are not imported.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] Every core canonical command and compatibility spelling resolves exactly one lazy handler through a closed adapter kind, and only the selected handler/parser modules are imported.\n- [x] The top-level router preserves original remainder argv and the selected S2 factory parses it exactly once; no route-level option grammar exists.\n- [x] Registry-derived mount/init behavior matches the pre-cutover census for every route, including no-auto-mount and conditional cases.\n- [x] Confirmation, global output extraction, legacy JSON shapes, `--`, streams, exit codes, and exception propagation match existing behavioral tests.\n- [x] Bridge compatibility spellings and hidden `bridge-status` execute through approved adapters while `purge-bridge` remains unknown.\n- [x] Execution can switch back to derived compatibility exports without handler, generated-help, or persisted-data changes.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/__init__.py","reason":"Replace execution ladder with selected lazy route dispatch."},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/_registry.py","reason":"Closed invocation adapter kinds and execution policy metadata."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_cli_registry_dispatch.py","reason":"New handler/selector/adapter dispatch tests."},{"path":"tests/interfaces/facades/test_cli_argparse.py","reason":"Real route, argv, stream, and exit behavior."},{"path":"tests/interfaces/facades/test_central_mount_gate_ad9f.py","reason":"Best-effort mount and no-auto-mount behavior."},{"path":"tests/interfaces/facades/test_cli_space_form_options.py","reason":"Global output and tokens-after-double-dash contracts."},{"path":"tests/interfaces/facades/test_leaf_writes_parity.py","reason":"Confirmation and legacy output parity."},{"path":"tests/interfaces/facades/test_bridge_vocabulary_heldout.py","reason":"Canonical and compatibility bridge dispatch."},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/_execute.py","reason":"New registry-driven executor: resolves the selected lazy handler and invokes it through the closed adapter-kind set with the route's init policy."},{"path":"tests/interfaces/contracts/test_bridge_vocabulary_stale_heldout.py","reason":"Categorize the new dispatch test file in the compatibility-spelling allowlist (it references bridge-fsck/bridge-probe census entries)."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","force_close_reason":"Plan-review staleness triggered only by a mechanical file_impact append (declaring the new executor src/rebar/_cli/_execute.py and the compatibility-allowlist test file I touched), not a material re-plan. The re-review BLOCK (G1G2) faults the plan for not enumerating Route.handler population, but it materializes the pre-implementation base SHA 9b1d2e6808 where all handlers are None; the landed change (Gerrit 1988, merged be8a60ba11, LLM-Review+1 and Verified+1) populates every core/bridge handler and passes the full held-out oracle — a provable stale-premise artifact of reviewing already-implemented code.","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["depends_on","2635-4aa3-5c14-4b12"],["parent","09ae-e827-1cac-452d"],["relates_to","1806-786a-1efc-484d"],["relates_to","2784-f69a-87db-4fb3"],["relates_to","90ce-d36c-2c79-4048"],["relates_to","b06c-04a9-52b2-42fe"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"09ae-e827-1cac-452d","parent_status_uuid":"c59478c4-0874-4422-b3a9-ebc602d20ad3","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":["rp05","cli"],"ticket_id":"e499-704e-fa13-4916","ticket_type":"story","title":"RP-05 S3 — Dispatch core CLI execution through validated lazy routes","verify_commands":[{"command":"env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/pytest -q tests/unit/test_cli_registry_dispatch.py tests/interfaces/facades/test_cli_argparse.py tests/interfaces/facades/test_central_mount_gate_ad9f.py tests/interfaces/facades/test_cli_space_form_options.py tests/interfaces/facades/test_leaf_writes_parity.py","dd_id":"AC1-AC3","dd_text":"Lazy route dispatch, mount/init, argv, output, and errors"},{"command":"env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/pytest -q tests/interfaces/facades/test_bridge_vocabulary_heldout.py tests/interfaces/facades/test_bridge_status_heldout.py tests/interfaces/contracts/test_help_overview_coverage.py","dd_id":"AC4-AC5","dd_text":"Bridge/retired vocabulary and compatibility rollback parity"}]},"source_event_uuids":["13dba065-23af-44a9-afc1-58ad7d214ea7","120ed879-cde0-48a6-9d3c-411c29a9